@startuml cumin-stop-after-runs
' cumin works - the stop after the current runs: cumin finishes the agent runs and starts no new work before it exits.
' Document: cumin-core.md, topic on the stop after the runs.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:Operator: cumin stop --after-current-runs;
:write stop-request.json
(state directory of the Host);
repeat
  :poll: read the request;
  :apply the actions that need no agent
  (requirement issue labels, labels of the pull request,
  merge after an approval of a Maintainer, close after a merge,
  stops for a Maintainer, follow-up notes, cleanup);
  note right
    Every start of an agent passes one check.
    While cumin stops, the check gives no permit:
    no agent starts, no label changes for the start,
    and nothing is counted. This holds for every
    request to an agent, at a poll and at the end
    of a run:
    split, acceptance check, claim, review,
    check fix, conflict resolution, review fix,
    fix of the review of a Maintainer, cause,
    and the second request of the split,
    of the acceptance check, of the implementation,
    of the review, and of the cause.
    ----
    The agent runs that are going on end
    by themselves. What follows the end
    of a run and needs no agent still runs:
    verify done, labels, merge, stops for a Maintainer.
  end note
repeat while (a run in progress before or after the poll,\nor one that the poll started?) is (yes: wait for the end\nof a run or the interval)
->no;
:remove stop-request.json;
:log "stopped", exit code 0;
stop

note right
  SIGTERM keeps its meaning at any time:
  cancel the runs and stop at once.
  A request that is found at the start
  of cumin run is removed.
end note
@enduml
